Found while coordinating the GH #55/56/58/59/60 batch, 2026-08-24. Verified by
reading src/config.rs on master @ 95d1d04. Pre-existing; not a regression.

## Two config ladders, opposite precedence

1. `UserPrefs::load` (src/config.rs:172-178) — user global FIRST, then
   workspace: **workspace wins**. Carries `default_mode`, `warnings_as_errors`.
   Its own doc comment still contains the unresolved note
   "(later wins? workspace should win)".
2. `LspConfig::load_with_parent` (src/config.rs:349-360) — parent config, then
   per-root config, then `load_user_config_file()` LAST: **user global wins**.
   Carries `openplanet_dir`, `plugins_dir`, `game_target`, `defines`,
   `source_paths`, `ignore_paths`, `shortcut_*`, `define_matrix`, ...

So a user-global `~/.config/openplanet-lsp/config.toml` with `source_paths` or
`defines` silently overrides a plugin's own `.openplanet-lsp.toml`. Every other
language tool (and the README's framing) puts project config above user config.
The layer-2b comment even documents the ladder as "parent config < per-root
config < user config", so the inversion is deliberate in code but almost
certainly not intended as UX.

## Impact
- A machine-wide `source_paths = ["src"]` breaks every plugin whose sources live
  elsewhere, with no local override possible.
- The two ladders disagree, so `warnings_as_errors` and `source_paths` obey
  opposite rules in the same file — undiscoverable without reading the source.
- New keys are landing around this: `unused_callbacks` (B012/GH #56) and
  `honor_gitignore` (B015/GH #60) both had to bypass the LspConfig ladder with a
  dedicated resolver to get workspace-wins. That workaround is now duplicated.

## Second, separate bug in the same area
`load_config_file` / `load_user_config_file` / `UserPrefs::apply_file` all do
`let Ok(cfg) = toml::from_str::<ConfigFile>(&contents) else { return }`. ONE
mistyped key (e.g. `source_paths = "src"` instead of `["src"]`) silently discards
the ENTIRE config file — every other key included — with no diagnostic. Users get
"my config does nothing" with no way to tell why.

## Work
- Decide the intended precedence (recommend: init options > CLI flag >
  per-root workspace > parent > user global > auto-detect) and make BOTH ladders
  obey it. Fold the per-key resolvers added for `unused_callbacks` /
  `honor_gitignore` back onto the shared path once it is correct.
- Report unparseable/mistyped config: keep the lenient per-key read so one bad
  key cannot nuke the file, and surface a diagnostic/warning naming the file, the
  key, and the expected type.
- Document the final ladder in README next to the config block.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Red: a workspace `.openplanet-lsp.toml` setting `source_paths = ["a"]` plus a
user-global setting `source_paths = ["b"]` must resolve to `["a"]` (fails today);
same for `defines`, `game_target`, `ignore_paths`. Variants: parent vs per-root in
a multi-root workspace; init options still highest; CLI flag still beats config;
one mistyped key leaves sibling keys in the SAME file effective (fails today);
malformed TOML still degrades to defaults without panicking. Precedence tests
must not mutate `$HOME` in-process (src/config.rs:1027 documents that as racy) —
use pure resolver helpers.

## Scope detail (from the B011 lane, 2026-08-24)

Every key `apply_config_file` handles inverts, not just the ones named above:
it is 15 unconditional `if let Some(x) = cfg.field { self.field = x }` writes —
openplanet_dir, plugins_dir, game_target, defines, source_paths, ignore_paths,
shortcut_namespaces, shortcut_disable_default_namespaces, shortcut_match_enums,
define_matrix, define_groups, define_combinations,
define_matrix_max_combinations.

The inversion matches its own doc comment (src/config.rs:316, 'parent config <
per-root config < user config'), so it is deliberate in this ladder rather than a
typo. The defect is that it is deliberately one way here and deliberately the
opposite in UserPrefs::load — a user-global `source_paths = ["src"]` silently
overrides every project's own value.

Whole-file-discard sites, precisely: src/config.rs:196 (UserPrefs::apply_file),
:519 (load_config_file), :529 (load_user_config_file). `game_target = 7` in a
config file therefore also disables source_paths, defines and the entire matrix
config, with no diagnostic, while the LSP appears to work.

Kept as ONE task rather than split: both defects live in the same ~20 lines of
config loading, and fixing precedence without fixing the silent discard would
leave the ladder correct but still untestable from a user's point of view.
The per-key resolvers added for unused_callbacks (B012) and honor_gitignore
(B015) both sidestep both defects by construction and should fold back onto the
shared path once it is correct.


## Note from B024 (2026-08-29)

The `defines` key no longer participates in the last-file-wins ladder at all:
config layers now ACCUMULATE their `defines` entries into
`LspConfig::define_overrides`, applied after target derivation and the
manifest (`-NAME` / `!NAME` removes). So the precedence work here should
treat `defines` as already resolved — the remaining inversion is
`openplanet_dir`, `plugins_dir`, `game_target`, `source_paths`,
`ignore_paths`, `shortcut_*` and the matrix keys. The whole-file-discard
defect is untouched by B024.

## Decision (coordinator, 2026-08-29) — precedence

Adopt the ladder the ticket recommends, both ladders obey it:

  init options > CLI flag > per-root workspace config > parent config > user global > auto-detect

Rationale: matches every other language tool and the README framing; project
config must be overridable locally. UserPrefs::load already has this shape
(workspace wins) — LspConfig::apply_config_file is the one that inverts.

Implementation shape: apply layers lowest-precedence-FIRST with unconditional
overwrite (user global, then parent, then per-root, then CLI, then init opts),
OR keep current order and switch apply_config_file to first-wins. Prefer the
former (apply in ascending precedence) — it reads correctly and keeps
apply_config_file a dumb overwrite.

Fold the per-key resolvers added for unused_callbacks (B012) and honor_gitignore
(B015) back onto the shared path once correct.

## Decision (coordinator) — lenient parsing

Parse into a per-key-tolerant shape so ONE bad key cannot discard the file.
Recommended: deserialize to toml::Table, then per-field try_into with the bad
key recorded as a ConfigIssue { file, key, expected, found }. Surface issues
through the existing diagnostic/warn path (stderr warn at minimum, LSP
window/showMessage if there is already such a channel). Malformed TOML (not
parseable at all) stays a whole-file skip, but must warn naming the file.

## Sequencing (coordinator)

B017 and B019 both edit src/config.rs and are run SERIAL in one worktree,
B017 first (it rewrites the ladder that B019's define gating sits in).